  "uprn": "10091693600",
  "decision_date": "20/10/2017",
  "description": "Prior Notification requirement under Part O of the GPDO for the change of use of offices (Class B1a)  to form 33 apartments.",
  "site_name": "Unit 3",
  "last_updated_by": "Northgate M3",
  "decision_target_date": "22/11/2017",
  "borough": "Hounslow",
  "postcode": "TW8 9RE",
  "street_name": "Riverbank Way",
  "bo_system": "Northgate M3",
  "development_type": "Notifications",
  "lapsed_date": "20/10/2020",
  "decision_conditions": [
    "Condition : 1 - The development hereby approved shall be completed within three years of the date of this granting of prior approval.",
    "Condition : 2 - No demolition or construction work shall take place on the site except between the hours of 8:00am to 6:00pm on Mondays to Friday and 9:00am to 1:00pm on Saturdays and none shall take place on Sundays and Public Holidays without the prior agreement of the Local Planning Authority.",
    "Condition : 3 - No development shall take place until a Construction Environmental Management Plan and Construction Logistics Plan covering both the demolition and construction stages has been submitted to and approved in writing by the Local Planning Authority. The plan shall cover:\r\na.\tParking of vehicles of site operatives and visitors; \r\nb.\tPedestrian and cyclist protection; \r\nc.\tProposed temporary traffic restrictions; \r\nd.\tArrangements for turning vehicles; \r\ne.\tThe routeing of vehicles to the site, access and egress arrangements and waiting areas;\r\nf.\tSafety measures and strategy to segregate school pupils and construction vehicle route to minimise risks of conflicts during its construction phase\r\ng.\tBoundary treatment and measures to ensure they are maintained in a secure and tidy condition; \r\nh.\tThe contractor's compound; \r\ni.\tNoise Mitigation measures in accordance with best practice as defined in BS 5528: Parts 1 and 2: 2009 Noise and Vibration Control on Construction and Open Sites (to be used to minimise noise disturbance from construction works). \r\nj.\tEither an undertaking to operate during all phases of demolition and construction a considerate contractor scheme in accordance with the Considerate Constructors' Scheme Code of Considerate Practice (see http://www.ccscheme.org.uk/index.php/company-registration/how-to-be-very-considerate/company-code-of-considerate-practice  or such other methods for achieving these objectives the details of which shall first have been submitted to and approved in writing by the local planning authority; \r\nAll work on site shall be carried out in accordance with the approved details.\r\n",
    "Condition : 4 - Prior to the first occupation of the flats hereby permitted, a Car Parking Management Plan (CMPM) shall be submitted to and approved in writing by the Local Planning Authority.\r\nThe CMPM shall include the following:\r\n\"\tMeasures to prevent parking in inappropriate locations.\r\n\"\tA plan showing the layout of car park, including details of Electric Vehicle charging points for the bays at a proportion no less than 20% Active and 20% passive, at least 10% of spaces demarked for disabled persons, and removal of the parking bay closest to the car park ramp.\r\n\"\tMeasures for confirming how the existing spaces over and above the proposed ratio of 0.5 will be removed.\r\n\"\tDetails of how the car parking spaces will be allocated and managed to ensure maximum use\r\nThe CMPM shall then be implemented in accordance with the approved details before first occupation of the development hereby approved and thereafter retained for use at all times without obstruction.",
    "Condition : 5 - Prior to the first occupation of the flats hereby permitted, full details of cycle parking provision (including enclosure details) shall be submitted to and approved in writing by the Local Planning Authority. The approved details shall conform to current guidance such as the TfL London Cycling Design Standards in design and layout, and be fully implemented and made available for use before the first occupation of the development hereby approved and thereafter retained for use at all times without obstruction.",
    "Condition : 6 - Prior to the first occupation of the flats hereby permitted, the local planning authority shall be informed of the agreed naming and numbering of the proposed dwellings so that arrangements can be put in place to ensure that, with the exception of Blue Badge holders, no resident of the development shall obtain a resident's parking permit.",
    "Condition : 7 - The use hereby permitted shall not be begun until details of the arrangements for storing of waste and recycled materials have been submitted to and approved by the Local Planning Authority.  The arrangements for storing waste and recycled materials shall not be carried out otherwise than in accordance with any approval given and shall be completed before any part of the accommodation hereby permitted is occupied.",
    "Condition : 8 - Prior to the first occupation of the flats hereby permitted, full details of both hard and soft landscape works have been submitted to and approved in writing by the local planning authority and these works shall be carried out as approved.  \r\nThese details shall include:\r\n\"\tFacilities for pedestrians (e.g. dropped kerbs)\r\n\"\tSafeguarding of potential future routes along and across the railway line to the south of the site\r\n",
    "Condition : 9 - Prior to the first occupation of any part of the development hereby approved a Delivery and Servicing Plan shall be submitted to and approved by the Local Planning Authority. The development shall be carried out in accordance with the approved details."
  ],
